.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA / re-verification before repair:\n\nStep 0(a): duplicate sweep found closed `94a3-1323-3497-4f59` (same title/plan, implementation already on current `origin/main`) and open duplicate `3691-d673-2e4b-413a`; this ticket remains the operator-assigned work item.\nStep 0(b): no version was quoted in the report; using `created_at=1788160411083998001` gives reported-against floor `5697f2e11179`. The only suspect-path change from that floor to current `origin/main` was `44ec1c2e6737` (async gate start), not a material-diagnostic change.\nStep 0(c): worktree `debug-0561` is at `8db373933654c7c21fa214565426f562ca55cd80`, equal to `origin/main`.\n\nConfirmed mechanism: bug 330c (`9ba1e90e3ccc`, ticket `330c-1c85-5bd4-48b5`) correctly normalized AC checkbox state out of the material fingerprint, making tick-only edits attestation-safe, but the attestation diagnostic surfaces still needed component-level data/reasons so a stale-material refusal could say what actually changed instead of the old fixed list. Current `origin/main` contains the broad 94a3 implementation, but the strengthened AC still found the exact misleading fixed-list literal surviving in runtime source prose (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py`), so the final repair removes that literal from `src/` and pins the grep to zero offenders.\n\nDefect legitimacy: defect / diagnostic regression. The ticket itself gives operator-approved intended behavior: every attestation error must say what changed, and tick-only AC checkbox edits must be safe. No gate outcome change is in scope.\n\nAttribution: `caused_by=330c-1c85-5bd4-48b5` as an unmet diagnostic obligation created when checkbox normalization changed the behavior without updating stale-material explanations enough to disambiguate checkbox-only vs material edits. I recorded the caused_by edge separately as well; the close will also pass `--caused-by`.","timestamp":1788218266393874535},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review PASS recorded after description compression (verified_at_sha 05be3a4dc6e48d982006cc5532904cd17add41eb). Implementation is in Gerrit change 2467; local validation: targeted material tests pass, lint/typecheck pass, full unit+integration run reached one environment failure in live Jira ACLI auth (test_delete_permission_probe), not code-related.","timestamp":1788222640693606001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 landed. Re-verified that the broad component-fingerprint implementation is present on current main; the remaining source AC failure was the exact historical stale diagnostic literal still present in runtime source prose. RED: strengthened the source-tree guard to require zero occurrences and observed failure on material_diff.py. GREEN: reworded that prose without changing any gate branch, verdict, threshold, or hash logic. Targeted plan-review suites passed (113 tests), focused material-diff suite passed, replication confirmed tick-only remains certified while description/file_impact/children edits name their changed component, sandboxed mutation restored the literal and returned the guard to RED, and make lint passed. Full unit+integration run only failed on live Jira ACLI auth for test_delete_permission_probe, classified environment/auth. Gerrit change 2467 reached LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1 and was submitted as merged commit 1d9193332139. Attribution: diagnostic regression / unmet obligation caused by 330c-1c85-5bd4-48b5 leaving stale explanations insufficiently disambiguated after checkbox normalization.","timestamp":1788224399989235721}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788160411083998001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3d4add26-f0dc-4a59-8419-c5436387eeff","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"330c-1c85-5bd4-48b5"},{"link_uuid":"4e9d505b-c153-4dc3-8ba9-0486f0a09d9f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"79f4-9a2a-460f-49ab"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThree agents on 2026-08-05 reported contradictory answers to whether ticking an Acceptance Criteria checkbox invalidates a plan-review attestation. The empirical behavior is settled: checkbox state is normalized out of the material fingerprint, so ticking boxes is attestation-safe. The defect is diagnostic: stale-attestation messages used a fixed, partly-fictional component list (`description/AC/file_impact/children`) and did not say what actually changed.\n\nOperator-approved scope: wherever rebar reports an attestation error, it must say WHAT CHANGED. No gate outcome changes are allowed: edits may only change reason strings for already-failing branches or add deterministic diagnostic manifest data. If a proposed change would alter a verdict, threshold, branch condition, or add an external dependency, stop and escalate.\n\n## Re-verified findings / root cause\n\n- The material basis is a composite sha256 over `ticket_id`, `description`, `file_impact`, `children`, plus `file_impact_scope` when declared none. AC item text lives inside `description`; there is no separate `AC` basis key.\n- Checkbox state is normalized (`[x]` / `[X]` -> `[ ]`) before hashing, so a tick-only edit does not stale an attestation. Item text remains material.\n- A composite hash is one-way; a stale-material branch cannot name the changed component unless the signed record carries prior per-component fingerprints. Legacy manifests without that data must degrade honestly.\n- Related `children` material is derived from other tickets' parent/relationship state, not just this ticket's event log; existing `plan-material-pin:` lines can still recover signed child id sets for legacy degradation.\n- Current origin/main already contains most of the intended 94a3 implementation. This ticket finishes and verifies the diagnostic contract, including the AC that the misleading fixed-list literal no longer remains in `src/`.\n\nDefect origin: bug 330c (`330c-1c85-5bd4-48b5`, commit `9ba1e90e3ccc`) correctly changed the behavior by normalizing checkbox state but left the old generic staleness explanations without component-level diagnostics. This is an unmet diagnostic obligation/regression against the gate message contract, not a gate behavior defect.\n\n## Repair plan\n\n1. Keep `pass1.py` untouched (near the 800-line cap). Put per-component hashing and explanations in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py`, single-sourced with the composite basis.\n2. Ensure `build_manifest` emits deterministic additive `material-part:` component records and `manifest_material_parts()` parses them leniently so malformed diagnostics cannot change verdicts.\n3. Ensure `compute_validity` uses `explain_material_change()` for both plan-review and completion-verifier `stale-material` reasons, and that `stale-reopened` names the signed/reopened timestamps.\n4. Ensure claim-gate unsigned advice names both remedies: `review-plan` for no review and `sign-review` for a passed review whose signature failed to persist.\n5. Ensure all attestation refusal surfaces either forward the computed reason or preserve equivalent diagnostics: generation, resign, completion child closure, CLI sign-aborted rendering, close-gate/claim-gate/status paths.\n6. Remove the exact misleading fixed-list literal from runtime source while preserving historical explanation in docs/tests without recreating the diagnostic message.\n7. Document in `docs/plan-review-gate.md` that ticking an AC checkbox is attestation-safe and that stale-material reasons name changed components.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py` — per-component hashing/explainer and removal of the exact misleading literal from source prose.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py` — additive material-part emit/parse behavior.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` — component-named stale-material reasons and timestamped stale-reopened.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py` — actionable unsigned message and accurate verdict vocabulary.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py` — named material/dependency staleness messages.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py` — named material staleness messages.\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion.py` — child closure validity reason forwarding.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py` — sign-aborted reason/remedy rendering.\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md` — checkbox-safety and component-diff documentation.\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py` — regression tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `material_components(ctx)` covers exactly the composite material basis keys; changing one basis component changes only that component hash.\n- [x] `build_manifest` emits sorted additive `material-part` records and `manifest_material_parts()` round-trips them; old manifests parse to `{}`.\n- [x] `stale-material` reasons name only the differing component(s) with compact magnitude and never report the fixed list `description/AC/file_impact/children`; grep proves that literal is gone from `src/`.\n- [x] Tick-only AC checkbox edits leave `compute_validity(...)[\"verdict\"] == \"certified\"`.\n- [x] Pre-330c legacy attestations over unchanged material remain certified; un-grandfatherable legacy attestations say the changed component cannot be named instead of inventing one.\n- [x] `stale-reopened` names both timestamps and unsigned claim-gate advice names both `review-plan` and `sign-review` remedies.\n- [x] `plan_review_sign_aborted` rendering includes its reason (for example `store-read-failure`) and does not advise `sign-review` for store-read failures.\n- [x] Dependency-material drift messages from generation name the changed dependency ticket ids, matching resign behavior.\n- [x] No gate outcomes change: touched stale branches keep their existing `(valid, verdict)` pairs, and targeted plan-review suites pass.\n- [x] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` states plainly that ticking an AC checkbox is attestation-safe.\n\n## Verification plan\n\n- RED: strengthen `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py::test_the_fixed_enumeration_is_gone_from_the_source_tree` to require zero occurrences of the fixed-list literal in `src/`; confirm it fails before the source cleanup.\n- GREEN: run `pytest -q tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py tests/unit/test_compute_validity.py tests/unit/test_legacy_material_grandfather_96d1.py tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py`.\n- Replicate: run a focused in-process script over `material_fingerprint` / `compute_validity` proving tick-only edits certify and description/file_impact/children edits produce named `stale-material` reasons.\n- Safety: run repo grep for the exact misleading literal under `src/`, docs grep for the checkbox-safety statement, and `make lint` / relevant type/test gates before Gerrit push.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py","reason":"new: per-component material hashing and the changed-component explainer"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py","reason":"emit and parse additive material-part: lines"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":"component-named stale-material reasons; timestamp-named stale-reopened"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py","reason":"actionable unsigned message; corrected verdict vocabulary docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py","reason":"replace the fixed-list wording; name the changed dependency ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py","reason":"replace the fixed-list staleness wording"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"forward the child-closure validity reason, not just the verdict"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"dedicated render branch for a sign-aborted failure naming its reason and remedy"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document that ticking a checkbox is attestation-safe and the new reasons"},{"path":"tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py","reason":"new: per-verdict message tests, 330c pin, legacy regression, gate-invariance"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","79f4-9a2a-460f-49ab"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"015a89d2-3b39-4b76-a7c2-af24923be4ab","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0561-20a5-87ba-4dcd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Whether ticking an AC checkbox invalidates a plan-review attestation is inconsistent across tickets","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8aa0281f-463a-4363-8a75-457860337e2c","2d8c2d90-85af-4746-a3ff-92bab65706f8","b0f36770-70f3-42ae-b185-243959116550","7d3bce28-1139-49ef-846d-56e49458cbf0","3d4add26-f0dc-4a59-8419-c5436387eeff","13fd1bed-3755-4aee-a3cb-8d84a6fe79e4","b7007b3b-5c71-426e-97d2-93c0ae334e4b","4e9d505b-c153-4dc3-8ba9-0486f0a09d9f","ff44ee8a-f782-418b-9d5b-70470131079f","0e2aff80-80df-47cb-9361-08cd525a1ddc","015a89d2-3b39-4b76-a7c2-af24923be4ab","b8d27c34-d3a5-4848-9980-4ca1f8b8a91c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788232967971924001,"uuid":"cee98168-708b-4c3f